  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Confounding by Weight Dynamics",
      "mechanism": "The study matched on *maximum* BMI, not current BMI or weight change. GLP-1 agonists cause significant weight loss, which is an independent protective factor for breast cancer. The observed 'protective' effect of the drug may be entirely attributable to the weight loss it induces, rather than a direct pharmacological effect on cancer risk. The control group, while matched on past peak weight, likely has a higher current BMI and less favorable weight trajectory than the treatment group.",
      "direction": "Biases the result towards a protective effect (lower odds ratio). The GLP-1 group is expected to have a lower current BMI than the control group. Since obesity is a risk factor for breast cancer, this difference in current adiposity creates a strong bias. The reported protective association (OR < 1) is consistent with this bias.",
      "evidence": [
        "Матчинг проводился по: ... максимальный BMI",
        "Матчинг НЕ проводился по: ... динамике веса"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "title": "Immortal Time Bias",
      "mechanism": "The study uses a retrospective design where exposure is defined as 'any prior or current use'. Patients in the GLP-1 group must have survived without a breast cancer diagnosis up until the point they received their first prescription. This period of survival is 'immortal time' that is incorrectly attributed to the exposed group's follow-up, artificially lowering their event rate. The use of logistic regression instead of a time-dependent survival model fails to account for this.",
      "direction": "Biases the result towards a protective effect (lower odds ratio). The event rate in the GLP-1 group is artificially deflated because it includes person-time during which, by definition, an event could not have occurred. The observed protective effect (OR < 1) is consistent with this bias.",
      "evidence": [
        "Дизайн. Ретроспективная когорта",
        "Определение экспозиции. Любое prior или current использование",
        "Time-to-event анализ не проводился"
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inappropriate Statistical Model",
      "mechanism": "The study analyzes data from a 3.5-year cohort using logistic regression, which is inappropriate for time-to-event data. This method ignores the timing of events and differential follow-up (censoring), treating a cancer diagnosed on day 1 the same as one on the last day of the study. A time-to-event analysis (e.g., Cox proportional hazards model) is the standard and correct method for such data.",
      "direction": "The direction of bias is indeterminate without individual-level data on follow-up times and event timing. However, the use of an incorrect statistical model invalidates the magnitude and precision of the reported odds ratio, making the result unreliable regardless of direction.",
      "evidence": [
        "Период наблюдения: 1 января 2022 — 30 июня 2025",
        "Метод оценки. Логистическая регрессия, оценка через odds ratio.",
        "Time-to-event анализ не проводился."
      ],
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "title": "Prevalent User Bias",
      "mechanism": "The study includes individuals with 'any prior or current use', which means many are prevalent users, not new users. Prevalent users are a selected group who have tolerated the drug and survived without major adverse events up to the point of study inclusion. This can make the treatment group appear healthier than the control group, independent of any drug effect.",
      "direction": "Biases the result towards a protective effect (lower odds ratio). The selected group of prevalent users is likely to have a lower background risk of adverse outcomes, including cancer. The observed protective effect (OR < 1) is consistent with this bias.",
      "evidence": [
        "Определение экспозиции. Любое prior или current использование агониста GLP-1",
        "Washout-период не применялся."
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    }
  ],
